Chapter: DeflateHostile
  cites Compress chapter Deflate

 Track D item 19, the Deflate half. Two shapes, and unlike Lz4 and Lz77 they
 fail differently from each other: one traps, the other never returns.

 Guarded because something runs it (red's ruling, 2026-08-16): `Brotli.codex:2408`
 calls `deflate-copy`, and `deflate-dynamic-test` round trips through
 `deflate-decompress`.

 Rows 1 to 5 are the positive controls, including the dynamic path, which is
 the one the loop guard sits in.

 Row 6 is the back-reference. `deflate-fixed-match:827` and
 `deflate-dyn-loop:900` both pass `list-length acc - dist` to `deflate-copy`,
 and `dist` comes off the stream through `dist-base`, which answers 24577 for
 code 29 and 32769 for code 30, both larger than any output a short stream has
 produced. It is called here DIRECTLY rather than through a crafted stream:
 hand-assembling bit-exact hostile Deflate is a separate job, and the value of
 this row is that it pins the guard where BOTH call sites and Brotli's third
 one land.

 Row 7 is the one that matters and it is not a crash. `br-bit:727` answers 0
 past the end of the input, so a dynamic block whose bytes run out mid-symbol
 keeps decoding zeros forever: `deflate-dyn-loop` never sees end-of-block,
 pushes a literal per pass and allocates without bound. `deflate-blocks:788`
 has an exhaustion check but it sits OUTSIDE the block loop, so nothing
 observes it once decoding of a dynamic block has begun. Ablated, this row
 does not print a wrong answer, it never prints at all.

Section: Helpers

  list-equal : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  list-equal (a) (b) (i) (len) =
    if i >= len then True
    else if list-at a i == list-at b i then list-equal a b (i + 1) len
    else False

  check-rt : List Integer, Text -> Text
  check-rt (input) (label) =
    let c = deflate-compress input
    in let d = deflate-decompress c
    in let ok = if list-length d == list-length input then list-equal input d 0 (list-length input) else False
    in label & "=" & if ok then "pass" else "fail"

  check-rt-dyn : List Integer, Text -> Text
  check-rt-dyn (input) (label) =
    let c = deflate-compress-dynamic input
    in let d = deflate-decompress c
    in let ok = if list-length d == list-length input then list-equal input d 0 (list-length input) else False
    in label & "=" & if ok then "pass" else "fail"

  make-repeated : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  make-repeated (val) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else make-repeated val n (i + 1) (list-push acc val)

 A skewed input, so the dynamic encoder has a reason to build a real table
 rather than falling back to the fixed block.

  make-skew : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  make-skew (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else make-skew n (i + 1) (list-push acc (if i - (i / 8) * 8 == 0 then 66 else 65))

  take-n : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  take-n (xs) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else if i >= list-length xs then acc
    else take-n xs n (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at xs i))

  show-len : List Integer, Text -> Text
  show-len (out) (label) = label & " len=" & show (list-length out)

 Row 7 reports a BOUND, not a length. The exact output of a truncated stream
 depends on where the cut lands in the table, so an exact number here would be
 an oracle copied from a run of the code under test rather than derived from
 anything. What the guard promises is that the walk stops when the bits do,
 and 10000 is far above what the remaining bits of a halved 400-byte stream
 can encode and far below the unbounded growth the ablated loop produces.

  show-bounded : List Integer, Text -> Text
  show-bounded (out) (label) =
    label & " terminated bounded=" & (if list-length out < 10000 then "True" else "False")

 The truncated stream keeps its dynamic header and loses the tail, so the
 tables build and the symbol decode runs out of bytes.

  truncated-dyn : List Integer
  truncated-dyn =
    let full = deflate-compress-dynamic (make-skew 400 0 [])
    in take-n full (list-length full / 2) 0 []

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (check-rt [] "1-empty")
    print-line-uni (check-rt [1, 2, 3] "2-tiny")
    print-line-uni (check-rt [65, 66, 67, 68, 65, 66, 67, 68, 65, 66, 67, 68] "3-repeating")
    print-line-uni (check-rt (make-repeated 42 100 0 []) "4-uniform-100")
    print-line-uni (check-rt-dyn (make-skew 400 0 []) "5-dynamic-skew")
    print-line-uni (show-len (deflate-copy [65, 66, 67] (0 - 24577) 3) "6-copy-negative-src")
    print-line-uni (show-bounded (deflate-decompress truncated-dyn) "7-truncated-dynamic")
  end

